DESCRIPTION:Arts & Crafts\, Children\n\nAges 5-9Have you ever wondered abo
 ut a beautiful painting you've seen hanging in the library? It's time to l
 earn more about the art that surrounds you every day!Start Arting by learn
 ing the basic concepts of art and seeing how they look in our library gall
 ery and on a famous painting. Then try it for yourself! This program will 
 have a hands-on art project involving paint. Please dress accordingly.This
  month\, we will learn about using colors with the help of Spatter Fish in
  the Lapp Story Silo and Greyed Rainbow by Jackson Pollock. How do the col
 ors make you feel? Do you like bright colors or dark colors? Which colors 
 will you use in your spatter painting?Registration will open at 9:00AM on 
 Wednesday\, October 21st for Manheim Township and East Lampeter residents 
 and on Wednesday\, October 28th for residents of other municipalities. Reg
 istration Requirements:  Please register ONLY the children who will be att
 ending. Accompanying Adults – This program is for adults and children 
 to enjoy together. Please plan to attend and be engaged with your child. D
 rop offs will not be permitted. No Show – Patrons failing to cancel th
 eir registration for more than 2 library programs in a month will be restr
 icted from registering for future programs for a period of one month’s t
 ime. Please cancel your registrations at least 2 hours prior to the start 
 of the program to allow those on the waiting list to be notified of their 
 change in registration status. Late Arrivals – Please arrive 10 minute
 s prior to the start of the program to allow for parking and other cir
 cumstances. The program will begin promptly at the designated time. At thi
 s time\, your spot will be forfeited to those on the wait list who will be
  granted entry. If spots remain\, registrants may be allowed into the prog
 ram. However\, registrants will not be permitted to enter the program 
 5 minutes past the start time. Cancellations- Please check your email prio
 r to departing to verify that the program has not been cancelled. Photogra
 phy - The Manheim Township Public Library Code of Conduct Policy prohibits
  photographing or video recording individuals (including children) without
  their consent (or in the case of a child\, the consent of a parent or gua
 rdian).
