 ogram where children ages 8-12 come together to build various creations us
 ing LEGO bricks. Participants often have the opportunity to work individua
 lly or in teams to design and construct imaginative structures\, vehicles\
 , and scenes based on a theme or their own imagination. The program typica
 lly fosters collaboration\, problem-solving\, and fine motor skills while 
 encouraging a love for building and creativity. It's a great way for commu
 nity members to socialize\, learn\, and have fun in a supportive environme
 nt.Registration for Lego Block Party will open at 9:00AM on Wednesday\, No
 vember 4th for Manheim Township and East Lampeter residents and on Wednesd
 ay\, November 11th for residents of other municipalities.For youth ages 8-
 12 years of age only.Designated Ages – Please adhere to the age restri
 ctions designated on your registration. Only children in that age range wi
 ll be admitted.   *Children ages 8 and older are welcome to attend the
  program independently. Cancellations- Please check your email prior to de
 parting to verify that the program has not been cancelled. Library Program
  PoliciesNo Show – Patrons failing to cancel their registration for more
  than 2 library programs in a month will be restricted from registering fo
 r future programs for a period of one month’s time. Please cancel your r
 egistrations at least 2 hours prior to the start of the program to allow f
 or those on the waiting list to be notified of their change in registratio
 n status.Late Arrivals – Please arrive 10 minutes prior to the start of 
 the program to allow for parking and other circumstances. The program will
  begin promptly at the designated time. At this time\, your spot will be f
 orfeited to those on the wait list who will be granted entry. If spots rem
 ain\, registrants may be allowed into the program. However\, registrants w
 ill not be permitted to enter the program 5 minutes past the start time.Ch
 eck In - All participants must provide an emergency contact number upon re
 gistration or at the start of the program.
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Morgan Center A
