BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Coffee & Crossing: Washington's Winter of 1776
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261214T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261214T194500
UID:a2fbea2cd9b3cb07aa1dbe6b0ae172ba@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Community\, Presentation\, Adults\, Seniors\n\nGrab a piping-h
 ot mug of authentic colonial coffee and step right into the high-stakes wi
 nter of 1776! Join living historian Samuel Leamer to uncover the bold stra
 tegy\, hidden Lancaster County connections\, and dramatic reality behind W
 ashington’s famous crossing of the Delaware and the epic 1st Battle of T
 renton. Separate fact from fiction\, sip historical brews\, and discover h
 ow coffee and courage helped turn the tide of the Revolutionary War!Regist
 ration is encouraged A Berks County native and Cairn University history gr
 aduate\, Sam Leamer has spent a lifetime bringing the past to life through
  reenactments-- and a decade mastering the art of modern coffee. By blendi
 ng historical scholarship with coffee expertise\, Sam offers a richer\, de
 eper look into Colonial Coffee Culture\, showing how the humble coffee bea
 n helped fuel America’s fight for independence.
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Morgan Center B
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/hold-adult-services-prog
 ram-200760
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
